  "status": "verified",
  "notes": "CSE-CIC-IDS2018 'Processed Traffic Data for ML Algorithms' day CSVs (CICFlowMeter), from the dataset's official public bucket. Verified on 2026-10-12 against the headers of all nine non-Tuesday day files: 80 columns = Dst Port, Protocol, Timestamp, 76 flow statistics, Label. These files have no IP or flow-ID columns, so events carry no source or destination. Dst Port and Protocol are kept as features but are also context: in a lab dataset a destination port can identify an attack scenario (a shortcut that may not transfer to real networks); the chronological study reports an ablation without them. Repeated header rows and rows with infinite values exist in the files and are rejected with reasons. Timestamps are as recorded by the dataset (dd/mm/yyyy, timezone not documented); they are parsed as UTC. Labels are the dataset's own, not analyst-confirmed.",
